I was tempted to use this comparison as well, but refrained from it
because "its" cannot be compared with "hers". It's a different type of
word.

You could say "its book" but not "hers book". In the latter case, it
should be "her book", which would make the example unintelligable. Also,
you could say "the book is hers", but not "the book is its".

